problems.problem:
Find all the pairs $(n, m)$ of positive integers which fulfil simultaneously the conditions:

i) the number $n$ is composite;

ii) if the numbers $d_1, d_2, \ldots, d_k$, $k \in \mathbb{N}^*$, are all the proper divisors of $n$, then the numbers $d_1 + 1, d_2 + 1, \ldots, d_k + 1$ are all the proper divisors of $m$.
